  "verbalization": "Yesanchinoside J is shown to have a target relationship with Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Yesanchinoside J interacts with T-24, which is a target of two different compounds: 1,5-dihydroxy-6-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyxanthen-9-one and Certonardoside I. Both of these compounds are linked to Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving this protein. Additionally, Yesanchinoside J is also shown to interact with T-24, which is a target of Sodium lauryl sulfate, another compound that also targets Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta. These findings suggest that Yesanchinoside J may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, possibly by modulating its activity or function. The evidence is consistent across different compounds, highlighting a potential role for this protein in the biological response to Yesanchinoside J.",
